Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: veltos-boot
Architecture: all
# grub-common must be configured before the preinst diverts its
# /etc/grub.d/10_linux; otherwise dpkg leaves the script as 10_linux.dpkg-new
# and the boot menu gets no VeltOS entry (install test, 2026-10-19).
Pre-Depends: grub-common,
             ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Depends: fonts-inter,
         pkexec,
         plymouth,
         plymouth-themes,
         python3,
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: libkscreen-bin
Description: VeltOS boot experience
 Makes start-up look like VeltOS from the first second:
  * "veltos" Plymouth theme (logo with a spinner, like Windows), made the
    default boot splash (plymouth's defaults file is diverted);
  * the login manager waits for the boot splash to finish;
  * "veltos" GRUB theme and boot defaults for installed systems: "VeltOS"
    menu entries, quiet boot with the splash, Windows and other systems
    detected for the boot menu.
  * the disk encryption password screen in the VeltOS style (font and
    Windows-like texts, set in the initramfs);
  * the boot menu and start-up screen at the screen's resolution: detected
    when VeltOS is installed, then kept at the resolution the screen is
    set to.
